<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong to tender HK$500 mln in 7-year notes.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong to tender HK$500 mln in 7-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority said it will tender HK$500 million in seven year Exchange Fund Notes on February 24 to settle on February 25.</p>
<p>Another HK$100 million in seven-year Exchange Fund Notes will be held in reserve for supply to market makers in the secondary market, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>The notes will mature on February 25, 2004 and carry a coupon of 6.46 percent payable semi-annually.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
